== Usage ==

Use this infobox at the start of an ability, spell, or weaponskill page. It
matches the style of [[Template:Item]] and [[Template:Mob]]. All fields are
optional. Blank fields hide their rows and mean unknown, not zero.

<pre>
{{Action
| icon =
| classes =
| level =
| cost =
| cast =
| recast =
| range =
| radius =
| damageclass =
| attacktype =
| element =
| target =
| aoe =
| castbar =
| damage =
| interruptible =
| status =
}}
</pre>

<code>icon</code> is the action's client icon ID. It selects the uploaded image
<code>File:XIVL_&lt;id&gt;.png</code>.

Include the unit in <code>cost</code>, such as "60 MP" or "1000 TP". Actions
can spend MP, TP, or HP, while some have no cost. Enter only numbers for
<code>cast</code>, <code>recast</code>, <code>range</code>, and
<code>radius</code>. The template adds their units. Range is the maximum
distance to the target. Radius describes the area around it.

<code>damageclass</code> identifies physical or magical damage.
<code>attacktype</code> identifies Slashing, Piercing, or Blunt damage.
<code>element</code> gives the elemental type. An action usually has an attack
type or an element, rarely both.

== Monster actions ==

Use <code>aoe</code>, <code>castbar</code>, <code>damage</code>,
<code>interruptible</code>, and <code>status</code> only on monster action
pages. These describe observed behavior that the client tables do not record.

* <code>aoe</code>: the effect's shape, such as "frontal cone" or "donut/ring AoE". Radius alone does not describe its shape.
* <code>castbar</code>: the cast bar's color. Red indicates damage, Purple a debuff, Yellow a buff, and Blue a special action.
* <code>interruptible</code>: whether stunning the caster stops the action.
* <code>status</code>: the status effect the action applies.

Use <code>damage</code> only when neither <code>damageclass</code> nor the cast
bar indicates whether the action deals damage. Omit it when another row
already answers that question.

== Numbered tiers ==

A 1.x action upgrades through tiers under the same action. Cure has nine tiers,
Protect has seven, and 170 of the 476 actions have at least two. Keep the tiers
on one page: describe the base action in the infobox and list its tiers in a
table below it.

<pre>
{| class="xiv-table altrow-blue wide-table"
! Tier !! Level !! Cost !! Recast
|-
| Cure || 4 || 24 MP || 2.5
|}
</pre>
